{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>You shall not gash yourselves.</b> Like the meaning of \"you shall not make any cut for a soul\" (Leviticus 19:28) — decreed upon all bands of raiders." "<b>And you shall not make a bald spot.</b> Like the practice of the nations, to this day." "And the meaning of <b>children.</b> Since you know that you are children to HaShem, and He loves you more than a father loves a son — do not gash yourselves over anything He does, for everything He does is for good. And if you do not understand it, just as small children do not understand the deed of their father but trust in Him — so you too shall do. For you are a holy people, and you are not like all the other nations; therefore do not do as their deeds. And the reason for the juxtaposition of the passage \"you shall not eat any abomination\" is: for you are a holy people in heart and mouth, and you shall be set apart from the peoples, and all who see you shall recognize you, for you shall not make a bald spot over the dead, and you shall not eat any living thing. And if you are a holy people, it is not fitting that you eat what is impure and defile the soul."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:23:24.283779087Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}